        name = "The Celestial Tournament",
        source = "The Celestial Tournament",
        sourceType = "Achievement",
        difficulty = "hard",
        difficultyReason = "Seven pet battles without out-of-battle healing require a prepared roster.",
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - Seven pet battles without out-of-battle healing require a prepared roster.\n\n1. Prepare at least fifteen level-25 pets, preferably a deeper rare-quality roster with spare teams. At Master Li on Timeless Isle 34.8,59.6 accept The Celestial Tournament (33137) and enter the solo scenario. Fifteen is the current entry requirement; the old thirty-pet beta requirement is obsolete.\n\n2. Inspect this week's three trainers. Rotation one is Cho / Dr. Ion Goldbloom / Sully; rotation two is Taran Zhu / Chen / Wrathion; rotation three is Wise Mari / Blingtron 4000 / Kiryn. Change teams between battles, but preserve enough healthy pets for four celestials afterward. Bandages and Revive Battle Pets cannot be used inside; pet healing abilities in combat can.\n\n3. For the trainer round, counter each enemy rather than taking one fixed team to all nine trainers: Undead attacks are strong against Taran Zhu's Humanoids; Humanoid attacks handle Wrathion's Dragonkin; Flying attacks handle Mari's Aquatic fish; Elemental attacks handle Blingtron's Mechanical threats. Watch defensive turns such as Decoy and avoid spending a major hit into them. Rebuild or bring a spare counter after a loss.\n\n4. After three wins, defeat Xu-Fu with Mechanical attacks and avoid Feed healing him; Call Lightning plus multi-hit Mechanical damage is useful. Defeat Zao with Mechanical damage while timing damage/avoidance around Wish and Charge, so a late heal does not undo your burst.\n\n5. Defeat Chi-Chi with Magic damage and avoid wasting strong attacks into Ethereal. Rapana Whelks/snails with Acidic Goo, Ooze Touch and Dive provide an accessible alternative. Defeat Yu'la with Humanoid damage and time Dodge or Deflection for Lift-Off's landing; Clock'em or a suitable Kun-Lai Runt can supply these tools.\n\n6. Win all seven battles within the same scenario attempt. Leaving resets the attempt. Return to Master Li and hand in the weekly quest for one Celestial Coin; on the first win also claim The Rainy Day is Here (33136) for two bonus coins. The first victory therefore buys one three-coin celestial pet immediately.",
