    [8536] = {
        achievementId = 8536,
        name = "No More Tears",
        source = "No More Tears",
        sourceType = "Achievement",
        difficulty = "medium",
        difficultyReason = "Root ten hostile puddles until they transform instead of reaching Immerseus.",
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - Root ten hostile puddles until they transform instead of reaching Immerseus.\n\n1. Enter Siege of Orgrimmar beneath the Vale's lake on Normal, Heroic or Mythic as permitted by this achievement's current tooltip. Do a full clear to reach the named boss; the Garrosh skip bypasses earlier encounters. Remove uncontrolled damage before any objective requiring the boss or adds to survive.\n\n2. Use Normal or Heroic; recent Mythic reports describe the puddles disappearing at reformation. Bring a druid with non-damaging Entangling Roots, or another control that actually stops a Sha Puddle without killing it.\n\n3. Damage Immerseus to trigger his split. Root HOSTILE dark Sha Puddles so they cannot reach the center, and maintain control until he reforms. A retained puddle then becomes a Tear of the Vale, which is the target you need.\n\n4. Let each transformed Tear engage/cast Cry, Cry, Cry for the conservative route, then kill it. Recent reports disagree on whether that cast remains necessary, so follow the tracked counter rather than counting every dark-puddle kill.\n\n5. Repeat splits until TEN genuine Tears have died and the criterion is ready, then finish the encounter. Killing ordinary puddles before they transform does not count, and ending the fight before ten loses the attempt.",
