    [8537] = {
        achievementId = 8537,
        name = "Strike!",
        source = "Strike!",
        sourceType = "Achievement",
        difficulty = "medium",
        difficultyReason = "One Iron Star must deliver the kill to at least eighteen gathered Warbringers.",
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - One Iron Star must deliver the kill to at least eighteen gathered Warbringers.\n\n1. Enter Siege of Orgrimmar beneath the Vale's lake on Normal, Heroic or Mythic as permitted by this achievement's current tooltip. Do a full clear to reach the named boss; the Garrosh skip bypasses earlier encounters. Remove uncontrolled damage before any objective requiring the boss or adds to survive.\n\n2. Body-pull Garrosh and keep him in the FIRST phase. Remove all passive damage, damage shields and modern automatic damage effects that could push him. Kill Siege Engineers on one side to prevent early stars while gathering, plus Farseer Wolf Riders and Desecrated Weapons with precise single-target attacks.\n\n3. Gather at least three six-Warbringer waves, preferably four for a margin. Keep the Warbringers alive and move them into the Iron Star's path near its wall impact. Leave the appropriate engineer alive when ready to launch a star.\n\n4. Current Midnight scaling reports say one star may not kill full-health adds. Let repeated stars weaken the SAME gathered pack until a single final star kills eighteen together. Keep killing Farseers/weapons without touching Garrosh or cleaving the pack.\n\n5. Once the eighteen-star-kill criterion is ready, defeat Garrosh through the remaining phases. Do not rely on killing the adds yourself while airborne as recommended by exploit-style comments; the normal repeated-star method has a successful 2026 report.",
